  "limits": [
    "Only building-web is exercised, with two tenancy edit/status scenarios and one MFA enrollment/recovery/disable scenario; not the full website or all portals.",
    "One Chromium worker and zero retries. All three scenario definitions are byte-identical to V3; only shared auth.tsx product source differs. No Firefox/WebKit matrix, Android, iOS, device, Codegen or load acceptance.",
    "MFA setup for the isolated administrator alias uses real enrollment/confirmation HTTP and TOTP; the UI manager performs the original full MFA scenario.",
    "A QA-only ESM startup entrypoint invokes the same application, restricted-role checks and event bus, then binds127.0.0.1; the product server.ts is preserved.",
    "The frontend consumer is freshly built in production mode; API and fixture execute with NODE_ENV=test on a disposable UUID database.",
    "Visual review means three screenshots and three sampled frames from each of three videos, not watching every frame or asserting exhaustive UX coverage.",
    "The raw MFA video remains private because the real scenario displays ephemeral recovery material. Only the two tenancy clips are eligible for reviewed public sharing; these are QA clips, not a complete product presentation.",
    "V1 preparation failure preceded database/browser execution and is preserved separately; it is not a failed product case or part of the three passing browser cases.",
    "V2 and V3 real2-pass/1-fail results remain preserved separately; V4 does not overwrite or reclassify either failed attempt as passing.",
    "Any separate authentication-renderer regression run has its own evidence and is not claimed or added to these three browser cases by this proof.",
    "No performance conclusion, production readiness, deployment, migration publication, commit or push is performed by this verifier."
  ],
